@startuml s_arbitration
!include _style.puml
title S — two buyers choose the same seats at the same moment

participant "Buyer A" as A
participant "Database" as DB
participant "Buyer B" as B

== S0 (READ COMMITTED) and S4 (SERIALIZABLE): identical SQL ==
A -> DB : SELECT seats 3,4 — free?  → yes
B -> DB : SELECT seats 3,4 — free?  → yes
A -> DB : UPDATE seats 3,4 SET held by A  (no condition)
B -> DB : UPDATE seats 3,4 SET held by B  … waits for A's row locks
A -> DB : COMMIT
alt S0 — READ COMMITTED (NEGATIVE CONTROL)
  DB --> B : 2 rows — **A's hold silently overwritten**; both were told "yours for 40 minutes"
else S4 — SERIALIZABLE
  DB --> B : SQLSTATE 40001 → retry → seats now held → choose again
end

== S1: one conditional UPDATE ==
A -> DB : UPDATE … WHERE seat IN (3,4) AND (available OR hold expired) → 2 rows, COMMIT
B -> DB : same statement → waits, re-checks the new rows → 0 rows → ROLLBACK, choose again

== S2: lock first ==
A -> DB : SELECT … ORDER BY seat_id FOR UPDATE → free → UPDATE → COMMIT
B -> DB : SELECT … FOR UPDATE → **waits** for A, then sees them held → choose again

== S3: lock first, NOWAIT ==
B -> DB : SELECT … FOR UPDATE NOWAIT → 55P03 at once → choose again

note over DB
  With marked seats nobody may skip the seat they chose:
  study 02's SKIP LOCKED does not apply.
end note
@enduml
